-### Work
+### Story
 
-**What it is:** A tracked piece of work in the team's tracker, in one of five types: **Feature**, **Story**, **Spike**, **Chore** and **Bug**. Each piece of work carries one ICE, and an ICE can have many pieces of work. A Feature carries its capability's ICE. Under a functionality, the Story builds it, and Spikes, Chores and Bugs sit under it; each carries the functionality's ICE. The issue carries a copy of its ICE; the ICE page holds the ICE itself. Work is not the capability or functionality — it is the order to build it.
+**What it is:** The work item that represents one Feature and delivers it, and with it that Feature's part of its Capability. When it is made, it reads its Feature's ICE and that Feature's Capability's ICE, and writes its own scope of work from them. It sits in exactly one Epic. There is one Story for each Feature in each Epic: when a later Slice includes a Feature again, that Slice's Epic gets its own Story for the Feature. It is not the Feature (the Feature is in the model; the Story stands for it in the tracker).
 **Who reads it:** both
-**Lives at:** the team's tracker (GitHub, Jira, Azure, Linear, custom), linked from its plan
+**Layer:** work
+**In the tracker as:** an issue labelled `work-item`
